==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|incumbrance}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|encombrance}}, from {{m|fro|encombrer}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that [[encumber]]s; a [[burden]] that must be [[carried]].
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders|8}}
#*: Some consideration was necessary to decide whether or not to leave his rifle there. On the return, carrying the girl and a pack, it would be added '''encumbrance'''{{...|; and after debating the matter he left the rifle leaning against the bench.}}
# {{label|en|legal}} an [[interest]], [[right]], [[burden]], or [[liability]] attached to a [[title]] of [[land]], such as a [[lien]] or [[mortgage]].

